Vendored MUI 3.8 developer-kit header subset
============================================

Source: Aminet dev/mui/mui38dev.lha (MagicUserInterface 3.8 developer files,
(c) Stefan Stuntz — freely distributable developer material). Only the
C headers are vendored (libraries/, proto/, clib/, inline/).

inline/muimaster.h is NOT the original: the 1997 file's multi-line asm
strings don't compile on modern GCC, so it was rewritten against
FD/muimaster_lib.fd using the NDK's LP* macros (same mechanism as the
toolchain's own inlines). Same LVOs, same behaviour.

Vendored here from amipkg's vendor/mui (same subset, same rewritten inline).

Used at COMPILE TIME only by agent/amimon-mui.c. muimaster.library is opened
at runtime and remains optional — the GadTools amimon covers systems without
MUI.
